[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station with rock bar as control. Informal Flat V installed 1972. Natural flow regime. GENERAL: Velocity area station with rock bar as control. Informal Flat V installed 1972. Station replaced 55005 Rhayader Groe (1937-69). Bankfull width 30m. No wingwalls/structure. STATION HYDROMETRY: Cableway span 54m. All but exceptional floods contained. Issues with stilling well intake pipe from 2006, notably affecting low flows, lead to long-term reliance on back-up recorder and culminated in eventual station rebuild in 2012/13. Following rebuild in July 2013, all ratings reviewed. Two peak flow ratings across period of record. FLOW RECORD: Flow series up to 1969 from 55005 Rhayader Groe; data generally thought to be of poorer quality. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8). FLOW REGIME: Only gauging station on the main River Wye that is unaffected by large water supply reservoir (flows from Elan Valley Reservoir complex enter the Wye just d/s).
CATCHMENT,Wet, upland catchment draining impermeable, metamorphosed Silurian sediments. High relief, headwaters reach over 600m, and feature steep sided valleys and high gradient streams. Dominant land use is grassland with moorland and extensive areas of forest in headwaters.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. Rating providing a good fit to gaugings.
Pooling Suitability,Gauged well above QMED and close to bank-full. Rating providing a good fit to gaugings.
[END]
